r decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.44 to \u22120.18), about \u22123.6\u00b0F since 1909. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1950s summers were the hottest in it.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 9 of 12 months. Highs rose in none; 8 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Bluefield's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.16 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 41.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 2004 (54.17 in); the driest, 1930 (27.00 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}